        "denialFound": "Yes. Adani Group, 31 Aug 2023: \"We categorically reject these recycled allegations. These news reports appear to be yet another concerted bid by Soros-funded interests supported by a section of the foreign media to revive the meritless Hindenburg report... we reject these reports in their entirety.\" The group said the claims rest on DRI over-invoicing cases closed a decade earlier, which reached finality in the SC in March 2023. Source: https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/adani-group-rejects-recycled-allegations-made-by-george-soros-funded-occrp/articleshow/103230293.cms . OCCRP's own article quotes Adani calling the allegations \"baseless and unsubstantiated\" and saying the listed entities \"are in compliance with all applicable laws including the regulation relating to public share holdings\". It also reports that Chang told the Guardian he \"knew nothing about any secret purchases\", and that Ahli and Vinod Adani did not respond. Everyone was asked. The existing contra edge enforce:c014 (the SC characterisation) also stands.",
        "innocentReading": "Ahli and Chang may be independent foreign investors who used their own money (OCCRP concedes \"There is no evidence that Chang and Ahli's money for their Adani Group investments came from the Adani family. The source of the funds is unknown\"). An advisory contract with an Excel/Vinod Adani entity would not by itself make them promoter-group 'persons acting in concert' under the minimum-public-shareholding rules. The SC held that such third-party reports are not conclusive proof. SEBI's FPI beneficial-ownership inquiry is the arbiter, and this file does not record an adverse finding from it.",
