          "1) text/d: replace \"this 'was not implemented'\" with \"per the FIR, this was not implemented 'according to the decision taken in the 48th board meeting' — i.e. a subsequent board meeting reversed it (BS: 'the 48th meeting reportedly reversed the decision') — and the contract went to Patel Engineering (2019); CBI alleges the process/e-tendering guidelines were irregular.\" 2) lab: change to \"Alleged: 48th board meeting reversed 47th-meeting re-tender decision; award to Patel Engineering under CBI investigation\". 3) benefit.how: change to \"Award under the continued tender after the board's 48th meeting reversed its own re-tender/reverse-auction decision (alleged irregular by CBI)\". 4) killIf: rewrite as \"Court finds the 48th-meeting reversal was validly taken on legitimate grounds\" (the rescission itself is already on record). 5) from: change \"2019-01-01\" to the 2022 FIR date (month or day not confirmed in these sources; use \"2022\"). Keep the 2019 award date in the text. 6) Consider putting the named officials (Choudhary, Babu, Mittal, Mishra) and Patel Engineering as the enforce subjects, or add their edges; CVPPPL itself is not a named accused. 7) Keep the tier at alleged. c058 stays, but note that exchange filings were not checkable (portals returned 403)."
