        "denialFound": "Yes, and it is a primary source. The Adani Group media statement of 21 Nov 2024 says: \"The allegations made by the US Department of Justice and the US Securities and Exchange Commission against directors of Adani Green are baseless and denied.\" It adds that the group will \"seek all possible legal recourse\". URL: https://www.adani.com/newsroom/media-releases/media-statement-1 . The repo also cites Forbes, 30 Nov 2024 (\"Adani decries 'baseless' US indictment\"): https://www.forbes.com/sites/tylerroush/2024/11/30/billionaire-gautam-adani-decries-baseless-us-indictment-accusing-him-of-250-million-bribery-scheme/ (403 to fetch, but already cited in other domain files). The contra lit:c018 is therefore wrong to say the denial was \"not captured\".",
        "innocentReading": "An indictment and a civil complaint are unproven allegations. The defendants deny them. DOJ under the current administration has reportedly moved to drop the criminal case, which may yet end without any adjudication on the merits. The state power-sale agreements behind the SECI manufacturing-linked tender were also signed by several states through the normal SECI intermediation process. Those signatures alone do not show bribery.",
        "reason": "Both sources I opened support the substance. The SEC press release is a primary record. It confirms the date (2024-11-20), the named actors, the \"hundreds of millions of dollars in bribes to Indian government officials\", the USD 750m September 2021 offering with about USD 175m from US investors, and the parallel EDNY charges. Wikipedia supports the \"over $250 million\" figure in the record's d field. An attributed indictment or complaint fits the 'alleged' tier exactly. The only defect is the required contra. lit:c018 says the denial was not captured, but a primary Adani Group denial exists and was reachable. The contra needs fixing; the claim itself is not refuted. Note that the existence of the proceeding is itself documented, from the SEC primary record. Only the bribery conduct is at the 'alleged' tier.",
