        "denialFound": "No direct denial of the report after publication was found. Reporters did ask: DH, \"In trouble, Reddys avoid media\" (https://www.deccanherald.com/content/179617/in-trouble-reddys-avoid-media.html), says the brothers avoided the press and met the CM privately. The cited source itself records their position before the report, which works as the contra: \"the two Reddy brothers, who have been claiming that their mining activity was confined to Andhra Pradesh and they were not involved in mining in Karnataka\" (https://www.tribuneindia.com/2011/20110728/main1.htm). Hegde is reported elsewhere as saying: \"They (OMC) may deny many times... But we have said they did engage in that through documents we produced.\"",
        "innocentReading": "Being \"named\" in a Lokayukta report is a recommendation from an ombudsman, not a finding by a court. The Lokayukta cannot prosecute on its own, and the report named about 890 companies and officials. So the edge on its own records only that he was named, not that he was guilty. The Reddys' position was that their mining was in Andhra Pradesh (OMC), not Karnataka.",
