        "denialFound": "FOUND, in the claim's own cited source. The claim says his denial was 'NOT captured in opened sources'; that is wrong. DH 27 Aug 2022 (https://www.deccanherald.com/national/east-and-northeast/storm-brewing-for-jharkhand-cm-soren-heres-what-we-know-so-far-1139789.html): \"In his defence, Soren has said that he had applied for the mining lease at a time when he was not holding any office of profit and he has now even surrendered the lease. Moreover, no mining activity has been undertaken by him in the mine in question, thus no question of misusing office of profit arises.\" The same article says that in an Interlocutory Application (IA) to the Supreme Court, Soren accused the PIL petitioner of trying to tarnish his image and said the PILs rested on false information. DH 25 Aug 2022 (https://www.deccanherald.com/india/ec-favours-disqualification-of-jharkhand-cm-soren-as-mla-raj-bhavan-sources-1139272.html) quotes his secretariat: 'No communication in this regard has been received by the Chief Minister's Office', and Soren: 'It seems that BJP leaders including a BJP MP and his puppet journalists have themselves drafted the ECI report'.",
        "innocentReading": "Soren may have applied for the lease, or had it renewed, before he held office. He says he surrendered it, and no mining took place. Section 9A covers contracts 'for the supply of goods to, or for the execution of any works undertaken by' the government. Whether a mining lease is such a contract is legally doubtful: Soren argued it is not, and the Governor never acted. The disqualification 'recommendation' rests only on unnamed Raj Bhavan sources, which the Raj Bhavan officially did not confirm, and a BJP MP (Nishikant Dubey) announced it in advance. The content of the opinion has never been verified.",
        "reason": "The central charge rests on anonymous sourcing, and the claim misstates its own evidence. DH 25 Aug: 'The Election Commission of India is believed to have told ... Governor Ramesh Bais that ... Soren should be disqualified ... Raj Bhavan sources said. However, Raj Bhavan has officially not confirmed the development.' DH 27 Aug frames it as 'speculation that the Election Commission has recommended'. That falls short of the 'reported' bar, which needs named sourcing or published documents. The self-allotment is an allegation by named parties (Raghubar Das/BJP; PIL petitioner Shivshankar Sharma), and a substantive contra exists in the cited DH article: applied before holding office, lease surrendered, no mining done. The claim says no denial was captured, which is false. Wikipedia is not independent; its only citation (ref 12) is the same DH 25 Aug report. The facts that do meet 'reported' are narrower: an s.9A notice was issued, hearings were held May–June 2022, and an opinion was sent in a sealed cover on 25 Aug 2022. The edge as written, with 'self-allotted' plus 'recommending disqualification', should be 'alleged' with a contra.",
