        "denialFound": "Yes, and it contradicts the claim. The New Indian Express, 27 Sep 2023, 'Iron ore mining agreement with Adani Group terminated in Chhattisgarh' (Prameela K, Raipur), https://www.newindianexpress.com/india/2023/Sep/27/iron-ore-mining-agreement-with-adani-group-terminated-in-chhattisgarh-2618757.html, quotes an Adani Group spokesperson: \"We have diligently fulfilled all our obligations since NMDC-CMDC Ltd awarded the contract for developing and operating Deposit-13 Iron Ore Block by NCL in 2018 through a transparent and competitive bidding process. However, considering the provisions of the agreement and the current circumstances, we choose not to comment at this time.\" FPJ separately reports: \"Adani Group's Raipur and Delhi offices did not respond to our request for comment on this cancellation.\"",
        "innocentReading": "In June 2019 tribal protests over the Nandraj hill stalled the project, and the Chhattisgarh government then halted the work. After that, neither party could move it forward. NCL cleaned up a non-starter contract, and each side blames the other for the failure: NCL calls Adani's reply 'mischievous', and Adani says it 'diligently fulfilled all obligations'. Neither account needs misconduct by the other side. It is a commercial dispute over a project blocked by protest and state action.",
        "reason": "The core event holds up. Two independent outlets (FPJ, and NIE with a separate byline and reporting) confirm the termination by the 2023-08-28 letter, the unsatisfactory show-cause reply, the 'shifting responsibilities' finding and the 'mischievous' quote from the CEO's termination order. But the claim states as fact that 'Adani did not respond to the reporter' and relies on c054 ('No public denial was found'). That is false. Adani gave NIE an on-record statement that it had 'diligently fulfilled all our obligations', which denies fault. The contra the claim relies on is incomplete, and the real denial is missing. There is a second problem. 'monopoly in operations' appears only in FPJ, as FPJ's own summary of the letter. NIE, which quotes the termination order directly, does not use it. So the phrase should not be presented as a quotation from the letter. The 'alleged' tier for NCL's characterisation of Adani's conduct is right once c054 carries the real denial. The bare fact of termination could separately be 'documented' (two independent outlets).",
