        "denialFound": "None found. Tata was asked and did not answer. Scroll (27 Nov 2025): \"Scroll sent questions to a spokesperson of Tata Sons about the timing of the donations to the BJP but had not received a response at the time of publication. Questions sent to the Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology...also went unanswered.\" Al Jazeera (18 Feb 2026, https://aljazeera.com/features/2026/2/18/quid-pro-quo-how-indian-firms-fund-parties-whose-governments-help-them): \"Al Jazeera reached out to the Tata Group, the Murugappa Group and the Election Commission of India ... but it has not yet received any response.\" That makes two outlets that asked and got no reply. c043 should cite both.",
        "innocentReading": "PET gives only in Lok Sabha election years: 2018-19 and 2024-25, with nothing in between. The April 2024 payment was made days before polling began, so the election calendar alone explains when it happened. The approval date is not needed to explain it. The 83% BJP share matches the 82% BJP share of all electoral-trust money in FY25, and the same payment also went to Congress, TMC, DMK and others. The semiconductor support is a published scheme that pays 50% of project cost to every approved applicant. The same Cabinet decision also approved a non-Tata unit, CG Power/Murugappa.",
        "reason": "The main sequence is real and sourced: the approval on 2024-02-29, the Rs 757.6 cr to BJP on 2024-04-02, and no reply from Tata or MeitY. As an analytic edge it needs no more than that. But the claim as written has two errors, and its innocent reading is wrong and misses the strongest explanation.\n(1) \"declared nil receipts FY21–FY24\": the source says no donations, and only from 2021-22 to 2023-24.\n(2) \"trusts were the only lawful corporate channel left\": this is false. Direct company donations under s.182 of the Companies Act 2013 were still lawful after the Supreme Court struck down electoral bonds on 2024-02-15.\nThe documented pattern that actually explains the timing is left out: PET has given money only in Lok Sabha election years, in 2018-19 and 2024-25. Once that is added, together with the 82% base rate for BJP's share of all trust money, the sequence says nothing specific about Tata. The edge can stay only as a correctly worded analytic sequence with the corrected innocent reading. The alternative is to demote it to context on the PET node. It must not be phrased so that the approval appears to explain the timing.",
