        "innocentReading": "This is ONGC's on-record explanation, not just ours. Bhubaneswar is the only oil-PSU SDI that has bought land and is building its own campus. The other SDIs (Kochi, Rae Bareli, Visakhapatnam, Ahmedabad, Guwahati) run from rented premises and so only need operating funds. The PSUs split costs by fixed shares (ONGC 15% of both operating and capital costs), with IOCL as the implementing agency. Vocational training is an explicit Schedule VII head. This explains why the money is concentrated. It does not explain why Bhubaneswar was the SDI chosen for a capital build while Pradhan held both the petroleum and the skill-development portfolios. That question is still open.",
