        "innocentReading": "India replaced CLND s.17(b) with the recourse model used in the international conventions: operator liability channelled to the operator, supplier recourse only by contract or for deliberate acts. The CSC and Vienna conventions use this model, and India ratified the CSC in 2016. The change applies to every domestic and foreign supplier. Its stated purpose (Budget 2025) is to bring in private and Indian capital. Foreign-incorporated companies are barred from holding licences. EDF's 2016 request is one of many vendor and industry requests for the convention-standard regime, not evidence that the provision was written for EDF.",
