        "innocentReading": "MEIL won the tender at ₹12,799.92 cr against L&T and BHEL. By its own June 2024 statement, reported by TNM and NDTV, it was the lowest bidder. The WNN article says it was selected under NPCIL's first use of QCBS for \"its strong technical approach and competitive pricing\", but WNN itself does not say L1. The tender began in May 2023, and technical bids opened in October 2023, before the bond disclosure and the FIR. The FIR concerns ~₹78 lakh in alleged bribes to NMDC/NISP/MECON officials on a ₹315 cr steel-plant works contract, which has nothing to do with nuclear work. An FIR alone does not debar a firm from central PSU tenders. MEIL's bonds went to at least nine parties: BJP, BRS, DMK, YSRCP, TDP and Congress, plus JD-S, Jana Sena and JD-U at ₹5–10 cr each, according to Tribune. That pattern fits hedging across incumbents.",
