        "denialFound": "Adani Power (The Wire, 7 Nov 2025) called R.K. Singh's claims \"entirely unfounded\", stemming from a \"misunderstanding\" of the project history: https://m.thewire.in/article/government/r-k-singh-blames-nitish-govt-for-rs-62000-crore-loss-in-adani-awarded-bhagalpur-power-project. Bihar Energy Minister Bijendra Prasad Yadav (ThePrint, 11 Nov 2025): \"The company that bid the lowest (amount) in the tender was selected. The decision was taken in the interest of the state.\" ThePrint also reports that Adani Power \"refused to respond to a detailed questionnaire\" (asked, no response): https://theprint.in/india/asked-bihar-govt-about-rs-62k-cr-power-plant-scam-was-told-all-hunky-dory-ex-union-minister-rk-singh/2780894/. These responses concern the overpricing allegation, not the award fact, which nobody disputes.",
        "innocentReading": "Bihar ran an open reverse e-auction with four bidders, and Adani Power bid lowest at Rs 6.075/kWh. The state signed a 25-year PSA with L1, as the competitive-bidding guidelines require. Recent new-build thermal tariffs have been in a similar range, and the nominal-rent land lease follows Bihar's 2025 industrial policy.",
