        "denialFound": "Adani Power (The Wire, 7 Nov 2025): the allegations are \"entirely unfounded\" and reflect \"a misunderstanding\" of the transparent process. It said \"certain electorally frustrated individuals and political interests are attempting to further a false and baseless narrative\", that it \"emerged as the lowest bidder, offering a tariff of Rs 6.075 per kWh\", and that \"the land had been leased rather than sold ... at a nominal rent, in line with the Bihar Industrial Investment Promotion Policy, 2025\". Bihar energy minister Bijendra Prasad Yadav (ThePrint, 11 Nov 2025): \"The company that bid the lowest (amount) in the tender was selected.\" According to ThePrint, the Adani spokesperson \"refused to respond to a detailed questionnaire\" from ThePrint. National Herald (4 Nov) says Adani \"has not yet issued any statement\", so it cannot back the contra. URL: https://m.thewire.in/article/government/r-k-singh-blames-nitish-govt-for-rs-62000-crore-loss-in-adani-awarded-bhagalpur-power-project",
        "innocentReading": "The tariff came out of an open competitive tariff-based bid won by the lowest bidder. A ₹4.165 fixed charge reflects the capital cost of a new 2,400 MW ultra-supercritical plant at 2025 prices. Singh's ₹2.75 benchmark is his own assumption and has not been tested against contemporaneous bids. Leasing the land at nominal rent follows the state's published 2025 industrial policy and is not a bespoke concession. The timing, days before polling, points to a political dispute inside the NDA as much as a procurement finding.",
