        "denialFound": "SECI CMD R.P. Gupta, 2024-11-21, as quoted by The Wire: 'There is nothing against SECI. It has done nothing wrong... There is no mention of any wrongdoing or irregularity on part of SECI.' SECI was asked and did not respond. The Wire wrote to SECI's CMD and said the story would be updated when a response came; none had arrived by publication (https://m.thewire.in/article/government/adani-bribery-did-seci-share-internal-documents-with-accused). AGEL's 2024-11-27 statement (BusinessToday) said the Adanis were not charged under the FCPA count. No denial found that addresses the specific claim about internal SECI documents.",
        "innocentReading": "SECI terminated Azure's 2.3 GW and substituted the other co-awardee under the same tender at the same tariff, through a supplemental agreement. When a contract is amended, the incoming counterparty routinely receives and marks up draft letters and agreements. Under that reading, 'obtaining and revising internal SECI documents' could describe normal counterparty review of drafts, not a leak. This reading is not ruled out, and no SECI officer has been named or charged.",
        "reason": "The quote checks out word for word in The Wire (22 Nov 2024), which reproduces the indictment: 'The defendants SAGAR R. ADANI and VNEET S. JAAIN and other Indian Energy Company personnel also secretly influenced the SECI process for reallocation of the 2.3 GW PPAs ... by obtaining and revising internal SECI documents.' The allegation comes from a named party (DOJ), is attributed, and has a contra (c055x), so it clears the bar for 'alleged'. Three field-level problems remain. (a) 'Implicates SECI officials' is The Wire's inference ('could not have accessed... without help from within SECI'); the indictment does not say it. (b) The target node treats AGEL as an enforcement defendant, which it was not. (c) The 2023 date window is wrong, and the dismissal with prejudice of these counts on 2026-08-10 is left out. None of these defeats the core claim that the indictment made this allegation.",
